append_md('SP61_CW_75_notes.md',r'''## Scan 018

Items ② and ③ compare the torsor description of `(G,E)`-structures with structures of a fixed type isomorphic to E. Item ④ is headed “Enveloppe vectorielle d’un polygône combinatoire.” It starts with the regular complex realization of a standard polygon and describes its dihedral action on the Euclidean plane. No date or page count; pencil archive number 17.

**Mathematics and reading.** The interlinear identity in item ③ has a small G/C-like initial. Its open form with a downward final tail also occurs in the unambiguous raised “G-ens.” in item ②, so G is preferred in `G=Aut_C(E)`; C remains an explicit alternative. This is a handwriting comparison, not replacement of a clear C because G is expected. The category alphabet is less securely distinguishable: plain and calligraphic C remain alternatives at the first occurrence. It will be reconciled with scan 017 during the second reading.

The exponential is written `i→exp(2iπ/n)=ζ^i`, with only one i in the numerator. No extra vertex-index factor is inserted. If the i in the exponential is the imaginary unit and the i in ζⁱ is a running vertex index, the notation conflates two roles; the sheet does not disambiguate them. “homothétie par ζⁱ” is retained as the author’s terminology for the written complex multiplication, without changing it to rotation.

**Authorial proof request.** The text says “il faut prouver que c’est bien une réalisation rectiligne si n≥3… !”; si n≥3 is inserted at the end. H’s “il faut prendre…” loses the request. A targeted check of the intended regular n-gon model is recorded as S018-POLYGON; it does not repair the displayed exponential. Both witnesses also give arrowheads to the two bottom sigma-row connectors, whereas the crop shows blunt bar-ended strokes.

The crowded bracket has only one identifiable est-like group at the end of a crossing stroke. Its state is doubtful. No second est is supplied to make the sentence grammatical.''')
